# Line endings, once, for the whole repository. Do not add narrower text/eol
# rules elsewhere -- this line is the entire policy.
#
# `text=auto` makes git inspect each file's actual bytes (the same
# NUL-byte/binary-content heuristic `file`/`diff` use) and decide for itself
# whether it is text or binary -- it does not depend on the extension, so a
# binary file with a misleading extension (e.g. a zip archive saved as
# `*.R-FILE` in tests/testthat/apis/) is still detected correctly with no
# entry needed here. Detected text files are stored with LF and checked out
# with LF on every platform, regardless of a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf -- this is what stops line-ending churn for good. Detected
# binary files are left untouched (no line-ending conversion, no text diff),
# which matters for tests/testthat/fixtures/, where fixtures are hashed
# byte-for-byte (file_hash = md5sum of the raw file): a binary fixture whose
# bytes get rewritten on checkout would silently break that hash.
* text=auto
